        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8bfe5da5-1e72-56b7-8f78-1042032bb42b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paul Collins, Blackie Lawless, Jack Lee, Peter Case\n- Bands: The Nerves, W.A.S.P., Blondie\n- Songs: “Hanging on the Telephone”\n- Places: New York City, Los Angeles\n- Topics: power pop, heavy metal\n\nFacts:\n- Paul Collins was born in 1956 in New York City and is an American writer, author, music producer, and multi-instrumentalist.\n- Blackie Lawless was born as Steven Edward Duren on September 4, 1956 and is an American songwriter and musician.\n- The Nerves were a mid-1970s American power pop trio based in Los Angeles featuring guitarist Jack Lee, bassist Peter Case, and drummer Paul Collins.\n- Blackie Lawless is best known as the lead singer and rhythm guitarist, and formerly bassist, for the heavy metal band W.A.S.P.\n- “Hanging on the Telephone” was first performed by The Nerves, a short-lived US West Coast power pop trio.\n- Later in 1978, Blondie recorded and released “Hanging on the Telephone” as a single.",
